      "nouns":[
         "When someone sneezes, to say 'Bless you!' in Russian you say 'Будь здоров!' (be healthy);\\nIf you ask someone a favor, you can start with a 'Будьте добры' (be kind);",
         "In English, nouns are inflected only based on their number (singular or plural) and whether it’s in the plain or possessive form.\\nRussian nouns are inflected(their ending changed) on gender, case, and number.",
